4. UPDATES AND SUPPORT
   (a) Corrective updates of the Core are provided at no charge until the
       later of (i) the end-of-life date of the Core's major version, which
       is twenty-four (24) months from that major version's release and is
       stated in the Core itself (VERSION file, start-up log), and (ii)
       twelve (12) months from delivery of the Delivered Work. The date
       that applies to an order is stated in its Addendum. A corrective
       update is one that restores behaviour the Core's changelog declares, or
       compatibility with a platform or runtime version listed in the
       Core's compatibility matrix; anything else is new functionality.
   (b) Corrective updates are delivered as a new release of the Core (a new wheel
       file) with its migrations, to be applied by rebuilding the deployment
       delivered with the Delivered Work.
   (c) Support (questions, configuration, diagnosis) is provided for six (6)
       months from delivery and may be extended for a fee.
   (d) New functionality of the Core (a later major version) is not included.
   (e) If, when the Licensee requests assistance, the Core is found to have
       been modified (by its manifest or otherwise), the Licensor's
       obligations under this Section end. The licence in Section 2 is not
       affected.

